.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Browse the organization’s assignments, spot gaps (outcomes, abilities, positions), and open an assignment to tighten expectations.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  = render "shared/maap/definition"
  %p.mb-3
    Assignments are the work people are accountable for. Clear outcomes and required activities are what make expectation alignment — and MAAP — possible.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Header
  %ul.mb-3
    %li
      %strong Assignments · List
      switches object and page type (Health, Insights).
    %li The info icon expands this help.
    %li
      The
      %i.bi.bi-plus
      button creates a new assignment.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 How to use the list
  %ul.mb-3
    %li Use Filter/Sort and Customize View to change departments, spotlights, and columns.
    %li Each row links to the assignment. Outcomes, abilities, and positions show what’s attached.
    %li
      Switch to
      %strong Health
      to see Expectation Alignment scores across assignments.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Example
  %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
    A row titled “Client Success Driver” with outcome badges, ability milestones, and “2 titles, 3 positions” means the assignment is wired into MAAP — open it to review outcomes and alignment.
